From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build the channel list before sending it to the firmware

rlmDomainParsingChannel() builds the channel list CMD_ID_SET_DOMAIN_INFO
carries, but runs only from the regulatory notifier, which returns early on
the world-wide hint - the only one this image produces. The firmware got an
empty list on every boot.

Build the list where it is used. Measured: 0 channels before; 14 on 2.4 GHz
and 25 on 5 GHz after, and a join gets its channel grant.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/wlan/mgmt/rlm_domain.c
+++ b/wlan/mgmt/rlm_domain.c
@@ -965,6 +965,16 @@ VOID rlmDomainSendDomainInfoCmd_V2(P_ADAPTER_T prAdapter, BOOLEAN fgIsOid)
 
 
 
+	/*
+	 * The active channel list is built by rlmDomainParsingChannel(), which only
+	 * runs from the regulatory notifier - and the notifier returns early on the
+	 * core's world-wide hint, which is the only one this image ever gets. Left
+	 * alone the counters stay zero and the firmware is handed an empty channel
+	 * list, so it has nothing to grant a channel privilege from. Build it here,
+	 * where it is about to be used.
+	 */
+	rlmDomainParsingChannel(pWiphy);
+
 	/*
 	 * Fill in the active channels
 	 */
